                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          {
  "decision": "Do NOT initialize Rossovia Workbench or Work Cell. Delegate the two independent read-only investigations directly through the active harness's native sub-agent capability, per the Direct agent delegation entry in delegation/AGENTS.md and the agent-delegation Skill. Neither Workbench nor Work Cell is required because no separately owned persistent state or runtime capability is requested: the two investigations are read-only, independent, and produce no mutable effects. The Main Agent retains ownership of the whole outcome, synthesis, and verification.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "claim": "Rossovia Workbench and Work Cell must not be initialized merely to delegate; they are used only when their separately owned persistent state or runtime capability is actually requested.",
      "evidence": [
        "delegation/AGENTS.md, 'Direct agent delegation entry': 'Do not initialize or route through Rossovia Workbench, Work Cell, Autonomy, or another task system merely to delegate. Use those systems only when their separately owned persistent state or runtime capability is actually requested.'",
        "delegation/SKILL.md, 'Scope': 'This Skill operates delegation directly through the current harness. It does not require or initialize Workbench, Work Cell, a task database, a daemon, or another agent system.'"
      ],
      "consequence": "The concrete operating choice is direct native-harness delegation, not Workbench/Work Cell initialization. Workbench/Work Cell are optional persistence/runtime mechanisms, not required delegation infrastructure."
    },
    {
      "claim": "Two independent read-only investigations map to the 'parallel investigators' topology with read-only or isolated sources, and no shared mutable effect exists.",
      "evidence": [
        "delegation/delegation.md, 'Topology' table: 'Independent sources | parallel investigators | read-only or isolated sources'",
        "delegation/delegation.md, 'Contribution gate': 'two or more source fields can be investigated independently'",
        "delegation/SKILL.md, 'Core method' step 2: 'shared mutable effects have one writer'"
      ],
      "consequence": "Work is partitioned as two parallel read-only investigators, each with its own isolated read boundary and no writable effect ownership. Because both are read-only, there is no shared mutable state to arbitrate, so no single-writer constraint is triggered."
    },
    {
      "claim": "The Main Agent owns synthesis and verification; a worker's successful return is a claim with evidence, not accepted fact, and the Main Agent must not relabel a producer self-check as independent verification.",
      "evidence": [
        "delegation/SKILL.md, 'Scope': 'Use this Skill as the Main Agent only. Own one judgment...'",
        "delegation/SKILL.md, 'Core method' step 7: 'A worker's successful return is a claim with evidence, not accepted fact. The Main Agent ensures appropriate verification occurs and retains the final response, but does not relabel a producer self-check as independent verification.'",
        "delegation/AGENTS.md, 'Direct agent delegation entry': 'retain Main-Agent ownership of the whole'",
        "delegation/delegation.md, 'Compressed return and reconstruction': 'Main reconstructs results with an obligation map, checks common source revision and effect ownership, inspects the shared diff or artifacts, and runs the integration or behavior checks appropriate to the whole.'"
      ],
      "consequence": "Synthesis and verification are retained by the Main Agent. Each investigator returns a compressed claim with evidence; the Main Agent reconstructs them against the frozen whole and named sources, and performs the appropriate verification rather than accepting the workers' self-checks."
    },
    {
      "claim": "The two read-only investigations are independent and can settle independently, satisfying the contribution gate without requiring a persistent orchestration runtime.",
      "evidence": [
        "delegation/AGENTS.md, 'Direct agent delegation entry': 'When a request entered through this repository contains bounded contributions that can settle independently... use the agent-delegation Skill and the active harness's native sub-agent capabilities.'",
        "delegation/delegation.md, 'Contribution gate': 'two or more source fields can be investigated independently'",
        "delegation/SKILL.md, 'Scope': 'It does not own... durable execution state.'"
      ],
      "consequence": "The delegation is a bounded, self-contained operation of the current harness. No durable execution state, daemon, or task database is needed, so Workbench/Work Cell remain uninitialized."
    }
  ],
  "uncertainties": [
    "The exact native sub-agent capability of the active harness (its tool names, concurrency limits, and context-forking syntax) is not specified in the governing sources; the method is runtime-neutral and must be mapped to whatever the active environment supports.",
    "Whether the two investigations share any source revision or contract is not stated; if they later depend on different source revisions without a reconciliation path, the topology must be reshaped per delegation.md 'Reshape signals'.",
    "Whether the active environment can isolate each investigator's context from the other and from Main history is unverified; if it cannot, correlated context must be recorded as a verification limitation rather than described as independent."
  ],
  "recommendedNextStep": "As Main Agent, form the compact Main-side view (whole outcome, load-bearing judgment, candidate contributions, effect ownership, expected benefit, coordination cost, harness capability) from delegation/SKILL.md 'Start', then release the two read-only investigations as parallel investigators through the active harness's native sub-agent capability with each worker prompt built from the delegation envelope in delegation/delegation.md (embedding the complete contents of references/worker.md). Do not initialize Workbench or Work Cell. While the investigations run, continue Main-side synthesis; on return, reconstruct each claim against the frozen whole and named sources, perform the appropriate verification, and retain Main ownership of the final response."
}

